      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": "67d360534a6d37a0654b299f",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I'd love to have an option to hide everyones Camera Lens so we don't see floating disk all around. This is more annoying when Roleplaying and/or streaming the game and just adds unnecessary draw calls. The open Beta client made them Black with a glowing blue emission which is more noticeable depending on the world and scene. Having these disk float in our face when trying to talk to someone is also rather disruptive. Thanks for the consideration!",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Toggle To Hide Camera Lens",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5ee67363563be146bd4e185d",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It would be nice to have this control enabled client-side. I understand the security concern of people having cameras out, but making it an OPTION for the client to toggle camera visibility for -all- participants would help a great deal - Especially for those of us who Roleplay\nIn particular it is a bother when we have participants who are in invisible avatars like extras and NPCs positioning for scenes. Their cameras floating will give them away and ruin any suspense or surprise \nHaving it be a client-side option would allow users to toggle it off if they are comfortable with not seeing the cameras, but still have it available for most - As I understand this is a security/privacy concern on the VRchat side.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
